ng to preempt anything but I  genuinely think from what we're seeing  the markets will probably dictate them  okay and my my final question to you you  were home secretary for three years  incredibly busy  insanely busy job and now you kind of  have stopped you're on the back benches  what's next for you do you want to go  back into government do you think you  might seek a career you had a successful  career before this or is your heart  always going to be in politics well look  it was the greatest honor it's the  greatest privilege to be home secretary  there's no doubt about that and toughest  job in government as well famously so  I'm a public yeah no doubt about that no  doubt about that you know you're  responsible for National Security there  are things that I know that many other  people never ever know  um and I was making life and death  decisions on a daily basis alongside  some of the issues that we've been  speaking about but even much wider than  that you know look at the legislation  that I've steered through Parliament the  changes that we made to migration should  be very weird so stop doing it well of  course of course but I am a public  servant first and foremost yes I had a  career previously but I chose to come  into public service and I and I do  believe it may be unfashionable to say  that I believe in serving my country and  that's what I hope to continue to do  okay principal thank you so much for  joining us on the show really appreciate  your time thank you thank you
 

